course: dictionary
lesson: 9843
title: One word, many jobs: switch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Switch can be a thing or an action, so check the words around it to find out which one it is. «Noah's tablet got so hot from a long game that it switched itself off.» Switched off is an action here, and the words it switched itself off after tell you it stopped working.
explain: «When something doesn't work, test the simple causes first: is the socket switched on, is the cable in?» Switched on means turned on, because you check whether the power is on. Try your meaning in the sentence: "is the socket turned on" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Switch can also mean to change or swap. «Many countries are switching off old copper phone lines.» Switching off means stopping them, and the word old tells you the lines are being replaced. When you are not sure, swap in a simple word like change or stop and see if the sentence still works.
fact: A switch is a small button or lever that turns a light or machine on or off.
fact: To switch is to change one thing for another, or to swap.
fact: To switch on or switch off means to start or stop a light or machine.
fact: A switch can also be a sudden change, like a switch from rain to sun.
fact: Never touch a switch with wet hands, because water can make electricity dangerous.
exercise: «Noah's tablet got so hot from a long game that it switched itself off.» What does switched off mean here? | Got a bigger screen | Ran faster | Was made of gold | *Turned off
exercise: «Inside your phone is a computer chip holding billions of tiny switches.» In this sentence, what are the switches? | Small toys | Pieces of sand | Phone covers | *Tiny parts that turn electricity on or off
exercise: Mia says the weather had a switch from rain to sun. What does switch mean here? | Something you sit on | A bag of sweets | *A sudden change from one thing to another | A slow walk home
test: Sam says, «Let's switch places, so you sit by the window.» What does switch places mean? | Run away | *Swap positions | Fall over | Turn the lights on
test: Why should you never touch a switch with wet hands? | Wet hands are too heavy | It makes the switch smell | *It could give you an electric shock | It turns the light pink
exam: Dad says, «Switch the lights off to save energy.» What does switch off mean here? | To sing | To fly | To wash the floor | *To stop a light working
